WEBVTT

00:00:00.354 --> 00:00:05.458
Expenses — Record what you spent for work, attach the receipt, and follow it until it's paid.

00:00:06.415 --> 00:00:11.519
The Expenses tab: the form at the top, and this month's expenses in the table below.

00:00:12.149 --> 00:00:15.553
Set the date and the time of the expense.

00:00:16.291 --> 00:00:22.397
Choose the expense type. Some types have a ceiling — an amount above it goes to your manager for approval.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:30.485
Most expenses are in money: pick the currency and type the amount. Some, like travel time, are counted in hours.

00:00:32.997 --> 00:00:39.102
If it was for a client, say which client, project and work order — it then shows against their budget.

00:00:42.826 --> 00:00:45.333
Describe it in a few words.

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:55.451
Attach the receipt — a photo or a PDF. Finance needs it to pay you back.

00:00:56.787 --> 00:00:58.998
Then Add expense.

00:01:01.897 --> 00:01:06.262
Here it is, with its receipt — click the clip to open it.

00:01:06.908 --> 00:01:13.410
Reimbursement follows it from Submitted to Approved and Paid. Managers and finance change it here; you see it update.

00:01:14.113 --> 00:01:17.729
You can edit or delete your expense until it's approved.

00:01:18.399 --> 00:01:24.005
Move between months; the total of what you see is on the right. Managers can filter by employee.

00:01:24.632 --> 00:01:28.050
This view and Everything export the expenses to Excel.

00:01:28.766 --> 00:01:33.380
Record · attach · get paid — Add the receipt while you still have it. More help: the Handbook → Expenses.
